---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { TrackerPreview } from '../../components/TrackerEditor';
---

<Layout
  title="Free Printable Trackers — Personalize & Download PDF | ChartsAI"
  description="Make a printable habit tracker for your desk, fridge or notebook. Customize your habits, choose weekly or monthly, and download a free A4 or US Letter PDF."
>
  <section class="container listing-intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE MORE INTENTIONAL</span><h1>
      Good days start<br /><em>with small things.</em>
    </h1><p>
      Thoughtful printables for the things you want to make time for. Pick a layout, add your words, and take
      a little intention offline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="container section listing-cards">
    <div class="printable-feature">
      <div class="card-preview tracker-preview">
        <span class="card-index">YOUR NEXT LITTLE ROUTINE</span><div class="mini-paper">
          <TrackerPreview
            config={{
              title: 'Small steps, good days.',
              habits: ['Read a little', 'Move my body', 'Make something', 'Step outside', 'Wind down early'],
              month: '2026-09',
              period: 'week',
              paper: 'a4',
              ink: false,
            }}
          />
        </div>
      </div><div class="feature-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">FREE · PERSONALIZABLE · READY TO PRINT</span><h2>
          Make room for<br />a good habit.
        </h2><p>
          Weekly or monthly. A4 or US Letter. Your habits, your title, and a little space to reflect. No
          account, email gate, or watermark.
        </p><a class="button" href="/printables/habit-tracker/">Make your habit tracker ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container prose-section">
    <h2>A printable that fits your life</h2><p>
      A habit tracker is a simple sheet with a row for each habit and a box for each day. Mark a box when you
      complete the action. This collection begins with one flexible habit tracker, including weekly and
      monthly layouts, personal labels and an ink-friendly option.
    </p><p>
      Prefer to explore numbers you already have? Our <a href="/charts/">free chart makers</a> turn pasted values
      and spreadsheet data into downloadable charts.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
